From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:50:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] kboot: enable a handed-over external DCP and its Type-C
 routes on the J604

dt_reserve_j713_dcpext() hands the T8132 external DCPs over by marking
each apple,t8132-dcpext node apple,t8132-dcpext-firmware-ready, opt-in
with chosen.asahi,j713-dcpext=1. On the J713, U-Boot carries the handoff
into the kernel's own device tree (aurora-silicon/u-boot #31).

The J604 boots the kernel's device tree, completed by this stage, as it
does for its internal display. There, a dcpext, its mailbox, its
firmware and display DARTs, the DISPEXTn power states and the dcpext's
Type-C display routes are disabled until handed over. Add a path for
such one-tree boards, T8132_PATH_DCPEXT_ENABLE (the J604 only): after
the handoff, enable each marked dcpext with those nodes, in one display
transaction. Each power domain on the chain must be firmware-owned with
#power-domain-cells = <0>; the piodma child stays disabled, as the kernel
enables PIODMA at runtime; a route is enabled only when the tree has it
"disabled". On any failure the tree is left as it was and the marker is
withdrawn, so the kernel gate stays closed. Nothing changes on the J713.

The J604 kernel ships the external display driver enabled, so on the
J604 the handoff runs without chosen.asahi,j713-dcpext=1 and the value 0
turns it off. Its other checks still apply (internal display handed
over, an apple,t8132-dcpext node, DISPEXTn powered by iBoot), and the
J713 stays opt-in.

What the path reads, J604 against J713 (ADT dumps): dcpext0/1,
dart-dcpext0/1 and dart-dispext0/1 have the same registers, interrupts
and segment names (32 of 32 values equal).

tests: test_j604_dcpext_enable (production functions, libfdt): one
marked dcpext enables exactly its nodes and routes; both marked enable
both; a domain that is not firmware-owned leaves that dcpext as it was
and withdraws its marker; no marker or marker 0 changes nothing; the
J713 is never enabled. test_j713_dcpext_ready gains the J604 cases:
handed over without the line and with any value but 0, not with 0, not
without the internal display handoff, not for an unpowered DISPEXT1;
the J713 stays opt-in.

Assisted-by: LLM
